      "problem": "Which of the following represents the level curves of $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}?$",
      "worked_solution": "The level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equations \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nNotice that the range of $f(x,y)$ is $[0,\\infty ).$ So, we will consider only level curves for $c\\ge 0.$\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} & =c \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={c}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives us a family of circles centered at the origin. Therefore, the correct graph is as follows:\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14247393/assets/413a11a52ed6a4fc76c2848867d664a63fce24dd39088cdd5826b576d8e7b09c.png)",
